00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:10.493
All right.

00:00:10.493 --> 00:00:13.321
Please welcome the incredible, talented,

00:00:13.321 --> 00:00:15.690
just, oh, he's so everything.

00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:16.770
I don't know where to begin.

00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:17.936
It's Nick Kroll.

00:00:17.936 --> 00:00:20.936
(audience cheering)

00:00:24.014 --> 00:00:27.194
It's hard to describe you.

00:00:27.194 --> 00:00:29.854
I'm like, oh my God.

00:00:29.854 --> 00:00:32.283
I'm so happy for your life.

00:00:32.283 --> 00:00:33.116
- Thank you.

00:00:33.116 --> 00:00:35.520
- I mean, how is being a dad?

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:37.110
I mean, what's-

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:38.130
- It's such a bummer.

00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:39.042
No.

00:00:39.042 --> 00:00:40.290
(audience laughs)

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:41.982
Has anyone ever come on
the show and done that?

00:00:41.982 --> 00:00:42.815
- By the way-

00:00:42.815 --> 00:00:43.648
- I regret it, Drew.

00:00:43.648 --> 00:00:45.750
Every day I regret it.

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:46.680
No, but it's been,

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:48.180
it has been amazing.

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:49.170
It's like a true,

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:50.700
like, true gift.

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:52.200
We have a very,

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:56.130
he's a really beautiful, good boy.

00:00:56.130 --> 00:00:58.440
And at this moment I'm like,

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:00.780
