00:01:08.237 --> 00:01:10.320
'Cause I am such a ham with my kids.

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:11.153
- For sure,

00:01:11.153 --> 00:01:12.971
and I do Jon Hamm for
the kids all the time.

00:01:12.971 --> 00:01:13.804
(audience laughs)

00:01:13.804 --> 00:01:15.240
No, but I definitely,

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:18.240
I mean, I'm desperate for his approval,

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:19.920
and I do the voices for him,

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:22.080
and I'll do a voice,

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:23.534
and I'll sort of, I'll be trying to-

00:01:23.534 --> 00:01:24.367
- Like what voice?

00:01:24.367 --> 00:01:25.200
Could you give us the voice?

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:26.033
- I'll do like-

00:01:26.033 --> 00:01:26.866
- Not to put you on the spot.

00:01:26.866 --> 00:01:27.699
- No, no, I'll do like,

00:01:27.699 --> 00:01:28.710
I'll give him an Elmo or you know,

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:30.300
and he doesn't even know who Elmo is.

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:31.500
But I'll just be talking to him

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:32.333
and I'll be like,

00:01:32.333 --> 00:01:34.200
"Hey, how are you doing?"

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:35.657
And, and he'll-

00:01:35.657 --> 00:01:36.490
(audience applauds)

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:37.323
- Oh my God, can you imagine

00:01:37.323 --> 00:01:39.510
what it's like to be Nick Kroll's kid?

00:01:39.510 --> 00:01:41.850
- And he'll, he literally will be like,

00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:43.350
and as soon as I do a voice like that,

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:44.376
he goes, "Hi."

00:01:44.376 --> 00:01:45.750
(audience laughs)

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:46.710
Like, he thinks, he's like,

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:48.270
someone else has walked into the room.

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:49.590
- Which is comedy in itself.

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:50.640
He's your straight man.

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:51.473
- Thank you.

00:01:51.473 --> 00:01:52.408
Yeah, that's what I tell him every day.

00:01:52.408 --> 00:01:53.730
(Drew laughs)

00:01:53.730 --> 00:01:55.290
But he's, no, it's really,

00:01:55.290 --> 00:01:58.000
there's no joy like hearing
the laughter of your child.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:01.357
It really is like, a truly...

00:02:01.357 --> 00:02:02.190
(audience applauding)

00:02:02.190 --> 00:02:04.860
- Now I was reading about your wife Lily.

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:05.693
- Yes.

00:02:05.693 --> 00:02:08.280
- And you guys met on a dating app?

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:09.113
- [Nick] Yes.

00:02:09.113 --> 00:02:10.770
- [Drew] Okay, this is so hopeful.

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:12.540
- [Nick] It is. She's-

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:13.830
- [Drew] Oh, she's so beautiful.

00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:14.663
- She's beautiful.

00:02:14.663 --> 00:02:15.690
She's a landscape designer

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:18.360
and a botanical installation artist.

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:19.193
- That's so sexy.

00:02:19.193 --> 00:02:22.036
- Yeah, she does like, truly amazing work.

00:02:22.036 --> 00:02:25.710
And we met because, as you know,

00:02:25.710 --> 00:02:27.150
it's like, when you come,

00:02:27.150 --> 00:02:28.530
when you're, when you have been

00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:30.360
in an industry for a
certain amount of time,

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:32.970
you end up feeling like
you've met everyone,

00:02:32.970 --> 00:02:35.580
and your world becomes
smaller and smaller.

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:38.250
And I got on this app

00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:40.140
to sort of try to meet people

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:43.204
that were outside of
my particular circles,

00:02:43.204 --> 00:02:45.760
and I ended up meeting Lily

00:02:46.770 --> 00:02:49.740
and we, I think she messaged me

00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:51.210
on like New Year's Eve.

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:53.190
Like, I don't know, 2018.

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:54.960
And then we chatted for a while

00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:57.209
and then finally met months later.

00:02:57.209 --> 00:02:59.010
And here we are.

00:02:59.010 --> 00:03:00.240
And then we, now we have,

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:01.140
we're married and have a child.

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:03.210
And so, it's beautiful.

00:03:03.210 --> 00:03:04.065
It's really great. Yeah.

00:03:04.065 --> 00:03:04.898
(audience applauds)

00:03:04.898 --> 00:03:07.560
- Now, Nick has got this
brilliant new standup special.

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:09.930
It is hilarious and incredibly personal.

00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:11.460
We have a clip. Take a look.

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:15.000
- I am wearing silk boxer shorts

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:18.566
like a businessman on
vacation in Hong Kong.

00:03:18.566 --> 00:03:19.650
(audience laughs)

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:23.943
Those slide right on down.

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:27.090
Lizzy looks over at me

00:03:27.090 --> 00:03:30.480
and she is now eye to eye

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:32.698
with my bald little cashew.

00:03:32.698 --> 00:03:35.340
(audience laughs)

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:37.860
She is horrified.

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:40.380
Jenny, the girl who pantsed me,

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:42.660
is mortified,

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:45.574
and I am now a comedian.

00:03:45.574 --> 00:03:46.680
(audience claps)

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:49.050
- What was it about this special that,

00:03:49.050 --> 00:03:50.805
did you have a north star

00:03:50.805 --> 00:03:53.880
of what you wanted this to be?

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:54.990
- This particular project,

00:03:54.990 --> 00:03:56.340
I hadn't done a standup special

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:57.780
in like, over a decade

00:03:57.780 --> 00:03:59.490
and I, you know,

00:03:59.490 --> 00:04:00.750
I had done a lot more like voices

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:01.710
and character stuff

00:04:01.710 --> 00:04:04.140
and I really wanted to
do a standup special

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:05.670
that felt much more personal.

00:04:05.670 --> 00:04:07.560
It was actually Lily, my wife,

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:08.557
when she was my girlfriend, she was like,

00:04:08.557 --> 00:04:10.080
"Why don't you do an hour,

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:10.913
why don't you go do a special?"

00:04:10.913 --> 00:04:12.459
And I was like, "Ah, that's for the other,

00:04:12.459 --> 00:04:13.950
that's for all my friends

00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:15.300
who are like, they're standups."

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:16.770
And then I sort of was
like, you know what?

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:17.603
I'm gonna do it.

00:04:17.603 --> 00:04:21.960
And I took a note from
what we had been doing

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:24.780
on "Big Mouth," which is this
animated show that I make

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:26.670
which is very personal

00:04:26.670 --> 00:04:28.230
and largely autobiographical

00:04:28.230 --> 00:04:31.230
and much more vulnerable than
anything I'd ever done before.

00:04:31.230 --> 00:04:33.330
And so, I tried to take that

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:34.320
to my standup special

00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:37.470
and sort of really talk
about where I am in my life.

00:04:37.470 --> 00:04:40.410
And then, so many things
in my life unfolded

00:04:40.410 --> 00:04:41.700
while I was making it.

00:04:41.700 --> 00:04:42.570
Like, the lockdown

00:04:42.570 --> 00:04:44.130
and getting married and having a child

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:45.090
and all of that

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:46.830
sort of informed the standup.

00:04:46.830 --> 00:04:50.490
And so that hour's a much more piece of,

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:52.920
I hope first and foremost, funny,

00:04:52.920 --> 00:04:56.122
but also very kind of honest
for where I am in my life.

00:04:56.122 --> 00:04:56.955
(Drew sighs)

00:04:56.955 --> 00:04:57.788
It's really great, yeah.

00:04:57.788 --> 00:04:58.621
(audience applauds)

00:04:58.621 --> 00:04:59.550
- We have to go to a
quick commercial break.

00:04:59.550 --> 00:05:01.110
Will you take us to break

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:03.750
as any character you would ever wanna do?

00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:05.548
I just love hearing you do your voices.

00:05:05.548 --> 00:05:07.530
- Okay, I'll, I could do

00:05:07.530 --> 00:05:09.405
maybe Gunter from "Sing."

00:05:09.405 --> 00:05:10.238
(Drew yelps)

00:05:10.238 --> 00:05:11.071
- Sorry. Okay.

00:05:11.071 --> 00:05:12.777
- Don't go anywhere.

00:05:12.777 --> 00:05:14.730
We're heading back in time

00:05:14.730 --> 00:05:17.877
to relive a little bit
of the seventh grade,

00:05:17.877 --> 00:05:19.894
and so, stick around.

00:05:19.894 --> 00:05:23.394
(upbeat percussive music)

